    "updated_at": "2025-07-14T17:07:14Z",
    "body": "I agree with @stevefaulkner, though for a slightly different reason.\n\nAs a screen reader user, I'm not sure that knowing if a text description is Human or AI generated is that useful in the scheme of things. Errors in human generated descriptions are not uncommon, and the quality of AI generated descriptions is improving all the time. Much also depends on the prompts used to generate the description.\n\nHaving a way to programmatically identify the origin of the description doesn't solve the essential problem in either case - knowing whether the description is an appropriate alternative or not. It might perhaps signal the amount of trust you're willing to place in the description, but deciding that requires a certain amount of knowledge about the mechanics of how these things work. That might be useful for the cogniscenti, but I suspect it would just add noise for most screen reader users.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
