    "body": "I think what would be a more meaningful consideration would be new attribute that splits up the literal description of an image (mostly provided by AI) and another to further explain the intent (mostly provided by humans that care). As a simple example:\n\nLiteral description: Film poster for Weekend at Bernie's. [continues with literal image description]\nImage intent: \"How I look after a week at work\"\n\nIn the future, maybe the literal description could be added as a meta-data of the image.",
