    "body": "Better to have a more generic attribute that identify that any kind of attribute that generate information for users like:\n\n- alt (for images)\n- aria-label (for everything)\n- title (for additional info, like \"open a new window\")\n\n\nis set by\n\n- \"machine\" – The alt text was generated automatically, e.g., by AI, computer vision, LLM or template logic.\n- \"human\" – The alt text was written or reviewed by a human.\n- \"unspecified\" or omitted – Origin is unknown or not declared (backward-compatible default).\n\nSo can be an attribute \"gen\" or \"author\",\n ",
