    "updated_at": "2025-07-15T15:00:39Z",
    "body": "> While I can understand the desire, I think that this will be another hidden piece of data that will not be used much or not used correctly, we have a hard enough time getting dev's to write `alt` text without adding additional requirements. Also the origin of lots of content is becoming AI generated (not just image descriptions) so would prefer a way to indicate content in general is ai generated. But do not know if this is practical.\n\nI would agree that the scope goes beyond alt attributes. This should be page-level IMHO, for example like this:\n\n`<meta name=\"ai-generated\" content=\"alt, ...\">`",
