    "created_at": "2025-07-16T14:27:17Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-07-16T14:27:17Z",
    "body": "I have a different objection but I agree with @LJWatson and @stevefaulkner. An origin attr provides an ethical escape hatch for unethical authors but only transparent to robots and AT users (assuming it gains support, which I'm dubious). There should always be visible disclaimers when AI generated content has not been reviewed by the resource's author. Once reviewed by the author, it's their content. They can't then say \"sorry about that, AI generated it, I'm not responsible.\" Slippery slopes.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
