    "created_at": "2025-07-16T14:29:17Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-07-16T14:30:56Z",
    "body": "While it's a nice idea, I agree with @stevefaulkner  and @LJWatson . I suspect the purpose of the alt-origin attribute would be to convey a sense of trustworthiness of the alt text — yet, this doesn't seem like the right way to do this. [The Authentic Web / CredWeb group](https://www.w3.org/community/credibility/) is working on topics like this. As AI-generated alt text evolves it might get better. As human-generated alt text evolved, has it improved? 😜  Any person who is developing web content is responsible for the content and if AI-generated alt text is part of the process, it is still on the individual to ensure it is of useful quality. Also, as @AutoSponge surfaced, what if the entire page is AI-generated? ",
